      "num_turns": 46,
      "result": "Implemented the persistent Rails URL shortener API with link creation, listing, lookup, redirects, and click tracking. `start.sh` applies pending migrations and starts the server in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; the README documents startup and the endpoints.\n\nVerified the API over HTTP: generated and custom codes, duplicate-code conflicts, validation and malformed-JSON errors, 404s, redirect location and click counts. I also restarted the server and confirmed the saved link persisted. The temporary test records were removed. `bundle check`, migration status, and Ruby/shell syntax checks passed.\n\nOne environment quirk: JSON 3.2.0 was incompatible with Rails’ JSON rendering, so I pinned the `json` gem below version 3.",
